#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""context: compact "environment factors" snapshot for goal building and autonomous decisions. No tokens.

  context                    refresh every source, write ~/.local/state/context/today.md + today.json
                             (cron 08:25 and 18:25); the slow Telegram step runs last
  context --no-telegram      skip the Telegram step
  context --only hn,weather  refresh just these sources (the rest come from the last snapshot)
  context --force            ignore the per-source cache TTLs
  context --show             print today.md

Sources (each optional, failing soft: error -> last good value marked "stale" for up to 48 h, else "error"):
  hn         Hacker News top 30 (official API): stories matching his interests + top 5 overall
  health     latest ~/reports/unraid/*.md (unraid-health's daily report; never re-runs the check)
  capacity   `unraid-capacity forecast` (local samples, no ssh)
  media      `media queue` (GET only)
  weather    home today/tomorrow (profile home.*; open-meteo; MeteoSwiss app API as fallback)
  reminders  `remind list`, next 7 days      deadlines  `deadlines list --days 7 --json`
  location   the vault's Home Assistant status feed: ONE `vault ha now --json` -> flag home |
             away | far (> 50 km from home) + age, the zone name, outside zones the distance band
             (< 5 / 5-50 / > 50 km) and the town if the phone geocodes, and "driving" from Android
             Auto (core.drive's rule: only while the feed is <= 60 min old). Coarse values computed INSIDE the vault; no coordinates, street or address ever reach this box.
             HA is never contacted from here. The exact place only through
             the vault with his ✅ (`vault raw request --source location`).
  calendar   placeholder: the Google Calendar MCP lives in my session ("read in session")
  telegram   only when `tgread status` shows a login: ONE `tgread summarize --hours <since last run> --no-text`, the
             vault's digest (counts, needs-you flags, dated plans, signal categories;
             checked values, never message text), as an async vault job collected with `vault job wait --json` in
             steps of <= 230 s until CONTEXT_TG_TIMEOUT; a job still running then is picked up by the next run (the
             vault keeps it 30 min). today.* get "9 chats, 143 msgs · 3 need you (2 reply, 1 decision) · plans: Sat
             17.10"; the signal categories (type, topic, date: enums only) go to signals.json (0600, rolling 14 days).

Files (0600) in ~/.local/state/context: today.md, today.json, signals.json, cache.json. `context --cleanup-private`
deletes stray telegram.md, signals.md or location.json files there (run it only after the owner's OK). signals.json is excluded from brain-backup and recall (and ~/.brain.git never includes ~/.local).
Env (tests): CONTEXT_STATE, CONTEXT_UNRAID_REPORTS, CONTEXT_HN_BASE,
CONTEXT_WEATHER_URL, CONTEXT_METEO_URL, CONTEXT_TG_TIMEOUT, CONTEXT_NOW (epoch).
"""
